mes>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Hepatocyte-derived cysteinyl-leukotrienes modulate vascular tone in experimental cirrhosis</article-title><source>Gastroenterology</source><year>2000</year><volume>119</volume><fpage>794</fpage><lpage>805</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10982774</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1053/gast.2000.17831</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B6"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cl&#x000e0;ria</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Jim&#x000e0;nez</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Arroyo V, Gin&#x000e0;s P, Rod&#x000e0;s J, Schrier RW</surname></name></person-group><article-title>Renal dysfunction and ascites in carbon tetrachloride-induced cirrhosis in rats</article-title><source>Ascites and renal dysfunction in liver disease</source><year>1999</year><publisher-name>Malden, MA: Blackwell Science</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Titos</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Chiang</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Serhan</surname><given-names>CN</given-names></name><name><surname>Romano</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Gaya</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Pueyo</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Cl&#x000e0;ria</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Hepatocytes are a rich source of novel aspirin-triggered 15-epi-lipoxin A<sub>4</sub></article-title><source>Am J Physiol</source><year>1999</year><volume>277</volume><fpage>C870</fpage><lpage>C877</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10564079</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Keppler</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Huber</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Baumert</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Leukotrienes as mediators in diseases of the liver</article-title><source>Semin Liv Dis</source><year>1988</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>357</fpage><lpage>366</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3062791</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>